<% content_for :title, "Getting Started · Household Tracker" %>
<article class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl space-y-8 pb-8 leading-relaxed">
  <div class="sticky top-0 z-10 -mx-4 border-b bg-white/95 px-4 py-2 text-sm backdrop-blur">
    <%= link_to "← Household Tracker", root_path, class: "font-medium text-blue-700 hover:underline" %>
  </div>
  <header class="space-y-1">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">Getting Started</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Set it up once in Chrome on your Android phone, and the daily bill reminders arrive on your phone.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">1. Accept the invitation</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>Open the invitation email (sent from Household Tracker's Gmail address; the first time, check spam too).</li>
      <li>Tap the link and choose "Create an account" with <strong>the email the invitation was sent to</strong>, or "Sign in" if you already have an account. Google sign-in works too, with a Google account on that same email.</li>
      <li>Tap "Accept" and you'll see the household's bills.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">2. Install it on your home screen</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>Open <code><%= request.host %></code> in <strong>Chrome</strong> on the phone and sign in.</li>
      <li>Tap "Install App" at the top, or Chrome's <strong>⋮ → Install app</strong> (on some phones "Add to Home screen").</li>
      <li>From now on, open it from the <strong>home-screen icon</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">3. Turn on notifications</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>Open the app from the icon and go to <%= link_to "My Account → Notifications", account_path(anchor: "notifications"), class: "text-blue-700 underline" %>.</li>
      <li>Make sure "Push" is ticked for the household and tap "Save".</li>
      <li>Tap "Enable notifications" and choose <strong>Allow</strong> when Chrome asks. "This browser" then shows it's on.</li>
      <li>To keep amounts off the lock screen, untick "Show bill names and amounts in notifications (lock screen)".</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">On a new phone, repeat steps 2 and 3 there. Remove the old phone under My Account → Devices.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">4. Keep notifications on time (recommended)</h2>
    <p>Android's battery saving can delay notifications. In the phone's <strong>Settings → Apps → Chrome → Battery</strong>, choose <strong>Unrestricted</strong> (names vary by brand). Don't clear Chrome's site data, or you'll need to enable notifications again.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">5. What you'll get each day</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>At most one combined reminder a day: bills due soon, due today or overdue. It comes at 09:00 by default; change "Reminder time" in My Account.</li>
      <li>The same reminder also arrives by email and in the 🔔 inbox.</li>
      <li>After paying, tap "Mark paid" on the bill and nobody gets reminded about it again.</li>
      <li>"Snooze" quiets one bill for a while, for you only.</li>
      <li>"Add photos" on a bill keeps a receipt. Location data is removed from photos.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">6. If something goes wrong</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li><strong>No notifications:</strong> open the app from the home screen and tap "Enable notifications" again in My Account. Email and 🔔 still have your reminders.</li>
      <li><strong>Lost phone:</strong> sign in on a computer and remove it under My Account → Devices, or ask the household owner to.</li>
      <li><strong>Anything else:</strong> ask the family member who invited you.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="text-sm"><%= link_to "Privacy policy", privacy_path, class: "text-blue-700 underline" %></p>
</article>
